{"results": [{"id": "FAM:SF-APPS-085", "score": 0.163, "document": "# FAM:SF-APPS-085 | Study family SF-APPS-085: Connector teammate-path quality Q_p split-half reliability\n- observed_research_question: Connector teammate-path quality Q_p split-half reliability\n- auto_outcome_status: untestable\n- observed_hypothesis: Connector quality Q_p (teammate-initiated on-off PPP gap) is a stable player-season attribute.\n- observed_result: Pearson r(Q_a,Q_b)=+0.215 p=0.0297; Spearman rho=+0.242. Spearman-Brown Q~0.355, S~0.278. Sign agreement 65.7% (67/102) binomial p=0.000996. ICC(player-season)=0.216 (78.4% within). Attenuation: even a perfect predictor  [cut; read_family for the full text]\n- auto_failure_mechanism: A_unanswerable (question not answerable with the data or design)\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:low_measurement_reliability\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:MEASURE_RELIABILITY\n- observed_failure_evidence: Split-half r=0.215 / SB 0.355 is too low to treat Q_p as a stable scoutable trait; most variance is within-player half-to-half.\n- observed_sample_and_power: n=102 connectors\n- auto_related_family: FAM:SF-APPS-086"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPA-005", "score": 0.133, "document": "# FAM:SF-APPA-005 | Study family SF-APPA-005: Defensive scheme change within game and across games (inferred labels)\n- observed_research_question: Defensive scheme change within game and across games (inferred labels)\n- auto_outcome_status: untestable\n- observed_hypothesis: Playoff defenses change scheme within games and between games, especially after the opponent ran a play type heavily.\n- observed_result: Within-game change 319/523 (61.0%); cross-game change 298/440 (67.7%); 103/104 units (99.0%) and 52/52 series show a change; transition matrices near-uniform.\n- auto_failure_mechanism: A_unanswerable (question not answerable with the data or design)\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:label_or_classification_error\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:LABEL_ERROR\n- observed_failure_evidence: Doc caveat: inferred label cannot separate real defensive adjustment from offense executing differently; near-uniform transition matrices consistent with label noise.\n- observed_sample_and_power: 523 cells; 440 pairs\n- auto_validation_status: no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPA-027", "score": 0.12, "document": "# FAM:SF-APPA-027 | Study family SF-APPA-027: Agent Test B: LLM counter selection vs deterministic BEST tier\n- observed_research_question: Agent Test B: LLM counter selection vs deterministic BEST tier\n- auto_outcome_status: untestable\n- observed_hypothesis: The LLM picks the same counter as the BEST tier, and when it disagrees it is right in H2.\n- observed_result: Agrees with BEST 1/3; picks AVOID 2/3; disagreements engine right 2/2; mean H2 PPP BEST 1.650, agent 1.154, AVOID 0.642.\n- auto_failure_mechanism: A_unanswerable (question not answerable with the data or design)\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:small_sample\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER\n- observed_failure_evidence: n=3 triggers; caveat says 230+ disagreements needed.\n- observed_sample_and_power: n=3\n- auto_validation_status: no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED\n- auto_related_family: FAM:SF-APPA-028\n- auto_related_family: FAM:SF-APPA-028\n- observed_method: 3 suppression triggers; H2 PPP as referee.\n- observed_verdict: inconclusive\n- observed_failure_type: A_unanswerable"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPA-046", "score": 0.118, "document": "# FAM:SF-APPA-046 | Study family SF-APPA-046: Adaptation vs generic counter (W4)\n- observed_research_question: Adaptation vs generic counter (W4)\n- auto_outcome_status: supported\n- observed_hypothesis: BEST-tier counters are suppression-specific rather than the team's generic best available play.\n- observed_result: BEST == generic best 78.3%; suppression-specific 21.7%. Defense suppressed generic-best 4.7% (73); then specific 39.7%. When supp != generic, still picks generic 79.2%. (off,def) counter changes by what was suppressed 48 [cut; read_family for the full text]\n- auto_failure_mechanism: D_positive (no failure: positive result)\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:small_sample\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER\n- observed_failure_evidence: 78.3% of ranked BEST counters are the generic best available; Rank adds value in ~20-22%, 39.7% when defense took the team's best.\n- observed_sample_and_power: n=1,539 W4 triggers; 1,466 (95.3%) had a better option already\n- auto_related_family: FAM:SF05\n- observed_verdict: supported"}], "n_results": 4}

